> ## 2. Encounter Cards
> 
> I’ll keep these system-light: use d20 to hit, single damage die, and AC as a “target to beat.” You can adjust on the fly.
> 
> Rules assumptions (adjust if you like):
> - PCs:
>   - Ekemon: 26 HP, +3 STR to melee, decent AC (say 15).
>   - Varkash: 40 HP, strong melee, similar AC.
> - Enemies:
>   - Attacks: d20 + attack bonus ≥ PC AC to hit.
>   - Damage: 1d4/1d6/1d8 depending on size/threat.
> 
> I’ll group encounters by where they show up.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### E1. Mine Bats (A2 Guard Tunnel)
> 
> **Use for:** First combat, low risk; can add a few extra later as “wandering.”
> 
> **Mine Bat (minor)**  
> - HP: 6  
> - AC: 12  
> - Attack: **Bite** +3 to hit, 1d4+1 damage  
> - Movement: Can fly; can’t grapple.  
> - Behaviour:
>   - They swoop at lights and loud noises.
>   - If 1–2 are dropped, the rest may flee deeper into the mine.
> 
> **Tuning:**  
> - **Easy:** 2–3 bats.  
> - **Moderate:** 4–5 bats (but have a few flee when bloodied).  
> 
> ---
> 
> ### E2. Mine Gremlins (A3 Junction / D3 Bridge)
> 
> Nasty-but-cartoonish creatures that like traps and pushing.
> 
> **Mine Gremlin**  
> - HP: 10  
> - AC: 13  
> - Attack: **Nasty Pickaxe** +4 to hit, 1d6+2 damage  
> - Special:
>   - **Sneaky Shove (Recharge on 5–6):** Instead of a normal attack, it tries to push a target:
>     - Roll d20 +4 vs target’s d20 + STR mod.
>     - If Gremlin wins, the target is shoved 5–10 ft (you narrate: off-balance, nearly off a bridge, etc.).
>   - **Cowardly:** If half the group is down or fleeing, remaining gremlins disengage and run.
> 
> **Typical groups:**
> - A3 Junction: 2 gremlins (plus cover from crates).  
> - D3 Bridge: 2–3 gremlins, mostly trying to **shove** PCs off the broken tracks rather than kill.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### E3. Cave Creepers (B2 Rubble Creep / D4 Echo Grotto)
> 
> Small burrowing lizards/bugs that live in the rubble.
> 
> **Cave Creeper**  
> - HP: 8  
> - AC: 13  
> - Attack: **Chomp** +3 to hit, 1d4+2 damage  
> - Special:
>   - **Burrow Dart:** Once per encounter, pops out of rubble to launch a surprise attack. First attack against a target has **advantage**.
> - Behaviour:
>   - Territorial, not evil.
>   - If 2 are knocked out, the rest scatter.
> 
> **Typical groups:**
> - B2 Rubble Creep: 3–4 creepers.  
> - D4 Echo Grotto: 1–2 creepers or just one “boss lizard” if needed.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### E4. Animated Tools (B4 Old Break Room)
> 
> Fun, quirky fight with flying picks and shovels.
> 
> **Animated Pickaxe**  
> - HP: 12  
> - AC: 14  
> - Attack: **Flying Chop** +4 to hit, 1d6+2 damage  
> - Special:
>   - **Splinter Shower (1×):** When reduced to 0 HP, explodes in splinters:
>     - Each creature within 5 ft: d20 vs 10; fail = 1d4 damage, success = no damage.
> 
> **Animated Shovel**  
> - HP: 9  
> - AC: 13  
> - Attack: **Clang Slam** +3 to hit, 1d4+2 damage  
> - Special:
>   - **Trip Swipe:** On a hit, target must roll d20 vs 10 or fall prone (lose next move action / disadvantage on next attack).
> 
> **Typical group:**
> - 1–2 pickaxes + 1–2 shovels (3–4 total animated tools).
> 
> ---
> 
> ### E5. Crystal Sprites (C3 Gem Cutters)
> 
> Glittery little beings; can be playful or hostile.
> 
> **Crystal Sprite**  
> - HP: 7  
> - AC: 15  
> - Attack: **Sparkling Dart** +4 to hit, 1d4+1 radiant damage  
> - Special:
>   - **Blinding Flash (1× total per encounter):** All creatures within 10 ft:
>     - d20 vs 10; fail = disadvantage on next attack, success = unaffected.
>   - **Phase Flicker:** Once per turn, can move through small gaps or thin crystal clusters—hard to chase.
> 
> **Behaviour:**
> - If spoken to kindly and not attacked, they may:
>   - Offer a tiny gem, or
>   - Give a hint about the chasm or Titan Chamber.
> - If attacked first: 3–4 sprites fight until half are down, then vanish into the crystals.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### E6. Wind Wisps (D2 Rope Bridge)
> 
> Tiny air elementals trying to knock people off the rope bridge.
> 
> **Wind Wisp**  
> - HP: 8  
> - AC: 14  
> - Attack: **Gust Slam** +4 to hit, 1d4+2 bludgeoning  
> - Special:
>   - **Bridge Push (Recharge 5–6):** Instead of damage, target makes d20 vs 10:
>     - Fail: staggered to edge, next turn must spend move to catch balance or risk falling (you can add another check).
>   - **Invisible Until Attack:** First round they’re just wind; then they appear as swirling air and dust.
> 
> **Typical group:**
> - 3–4 wisps; they spread around the bridge.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### E7. Lesser Earth Elementals (E2 Titan Chamber)
> 
> The main guardians. You can run them straight or mix in a “solve, don’t kill” angle.
> 
> **Lesser Earth Elemental**  
> - HP: 24  
> - AC: 15  
> - Attack: **Rocky Slam** +5 to hit, 1d8+3 damage  
> - Special:
>   - **Shove Strike:** On a hit, can choose to knock target back 5 ft instead of dealing damage.
>   - **Rocky Shield (1× per fight):** On its turn, can hunker down; until start of next turn:
>     - Gain +2 AC and resistance to weapon damage, but cannot move.
>   - **Reform:** When reduced to 0 HP the first time, it crumbles. After 2 rounds, it re-forms at 10 HP unless:
>     - PCs use loud quake/fire (Fire Breath, collapsing a pillar, etc.) to “disrupt” the stones.
> - Behaviour:
>   - They protect the Scale, not out to kill; focus on **blocking** and **pushing away**.
>   - If Ekemon grabs the Scale and clearly backs off, they may stop and sink back into the floor.
> 
> **Typical encounter:**
> - 2 elementals.
> - To soften: let one join 1–2 rounds later, or have them focus attacks on Varkash, with Ekemon doing clever things.
> 
> ---
