> ### E8. Optional “Boss Plus Adds” Variant (Titan Chamber, if you want more challenge)
> 
> If combat is going very easily and he loves it, you can add small helpers:
> 
> **Stone Shardling**  
> - HP: 6  
> - AC: 13  
> - Attack: **Shard Stab** +3 to hit, 1d4+1 damage  
> - Special:
>   - **Merge:** If adjacent to a Lesser Earth Elemental, can merge into it, healing it for 4 HP instead of attacking.
> 
> Use 2–3 shardlings that pop out of cracks when the first elemental reforms.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### E9. Tunnel Vermin (Rats / Filler Fights)
> 
> Use anywhere you want a quick skirmish (A3, B1, random side rooms).
> 
> **Giant Rat**  
> - HP: 5  
> - AC: 12  
> - Attack: **Bite** +3 to hit, 1d4+1 damage  
> - Behaviour:
>   - Weak, easily scared; run if 1–2 are down.
> - Group size:
>   - 3–6 as a “mob” encounter; you can resolve two at a time to keep it brisk.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### E10. “Wandering” Howl or Miniquake (Non-combat but tense)
> 
> You can drop these in any tunnel if you want tension without combat:
> 
> - **Howling Wind Surge:**  
>   - Lights flicker, dust swirls; ask for a simple d20 vs 8–10 check to stay sure-footed.
>   - On fail, they stumble or drop something—but don’t fall far or take heavy damage unless you want to.
> - **Mini-Quake:**  
>   - PCs roll d20 vs 10:
>     - On fail, 1d4 damage from falling pebbles; maybe a side tunnel opens/closes.
> 
